From 0c1312f7d6fb78f24da264d7fb656f332fccb464 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Octo <180629317+OctoAlgo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:56:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] VICTORY_NATIVES: call the title's script natives from
 the debug channel

GTA VI 1.0.2.1 has no natives table: each of the 6820 handlers holds its own 64-bit hash
(`cmp dword [rcx+10h], 0` ... `movabs r, hash ; mov [args], r`), and scripts call them by code
offset from the interpreter's NATIVE opcode (+0x3de7411). VICTORY_NATIVES=1|trace|log (diagnostics
build, title executable of that build only):
 * finds the handlers by that shape through the image's function table (6820 expected);
 * replaces the opcode's `lea rcx, [rsp+0A8h] ; vzeroupper ; call r15` at +0x3de7503 (14 bytes,
   checked, logged) with a call to a stub near the image that hands context, handler and script
   context to natives::dispatch, which runs the queued calls and then the script's own native: a
   queued call runs on a script thread inside a script's update;
 * trace: per native the call count and the first three calls' arguments and results, marks every
   25 world frames, per-script and per-thread counts; log: every call; nwatchmem: which native
   changes a range of the image's data.
Debug channel: ncall <NAME|0xhash|+0xrva> [ret=<n>] [><var>] <args> (ints, floats, s:TEXT, h:TEXT,
v:x,y,z, $var, buf:<n>), npos, ntp, ntime, nstat, ntrace, ndump, nlog, nmark, nwatch, nwatchmem,
nscript, nfind; `done` waits for the results. Names: VICTORY_NATIVES_NAMES (NAME 0x<hash> lines).
The channel's img+ addresses now work (the loader tells it where the title is mapped).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
